.TITLE "uniq"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Reports or filters out repeated lines in a file. It identifies __duplicate entries__ and is typically used on sorted input to clean or analyze data.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**uniq file**
Removes adjacent duplicate lines from a file and displays the unique output.
> __file__ the target path

**uniq -c file**
Prefixes each line with the number of times it occurred in the input.
> __-c__ count flag

**uniq -d file**
Displays only the lines that were repeated in the original input.
> __-d__ duplicate flag

**uniq -u file**
Displays only the lines that were completely unique in the original input.
> __-u__ unique flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __uniq__ command only identifies duplicates that are adjacent. For this reason, it is almost always preceded by the __sort__ command in a pipeline to ensure all identical lines are grouped together.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:sort** **mac:grep**

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/uniq.html__
